; Tutorial_6_Convert_Slides_and_Spreadsheets.inix -- convert slides and spreadsheets

[about]
Title=6 - Convert Slides and Spreadsheets
Intro=Converting PowerPoint slides and Excel workbooks into web pages, and how each is laid out for reading.
Setup=A presentation or a workbook of your own, and Microsoft Office installed.
Homework=Convert a slide deck, then move through it by heading, one slide at a time.

[step]

Say=One want: the slides from a talk I missed, and the budget workbook shared with it, both readable without opening PowerPoint or Excel.
Key=

[step]

Say=I open the dialog. Source files can hold several files at once, separated by spaces.
Key=Alt+Control+2
Hear=2htm dialog
Hear=Source files edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type both names, each in quotation marks because they contain spaces.
Key=
Hear=quote Talk dot pptx quote quote Budget dot xlsx quote
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter converts both. PowerPoint and Excel read them in the background.
Key=Enter
Hear=2 files converted
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I open the slides' page. Each slide is a section with its title as a heading.
Key=
Hear=Talk, heading level 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=H moves slide by slide.
Key=H
Hear=Slide 2, Our goals, heading level 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Under each heading come the slide's words, then its speaker notes, so what the presenter said is there too.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Notes: start with the year in review
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Pictures on a slide read their descriptions, if the author wrote them.
Key=G
Hear=graphic, Map of the new offices
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now the workbook's page. Each sheet becomes a section with the sheet's name as its heading.
Key=
Hear=Budget, heading level 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Under it, the sheet's cells are a table, so the reader's table keys move by row and column, and each cell is read with its column's heading.
Key=T
Hear=table with 5 columns and 12 rows
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus Down Arrow moves down a column.
Key=Alt+Control+Down Arrow
Hear=Amount, 1,200
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Formulas arrive as the values they show, which is what a reader of the page wants.
Key=

[step]

Say=A very wide sheet reads best with the screen reader's table commands, rather than line by line.
Key=

[step]

Say=A chart in a slide reads the description its author wrote; with none, it reads as a graphic with no name, which is worth telling the author.
Key=

[step]

Say=Slides with several text boxes keep them in reading order, the order a screen reader meets them in PowerPoint itself.
Key=

[step]

Say=A workbook's hidden sheets are not converted, so the page holds only what its author shows.
Key=

[step]

Say=Merged cells keep their place in the table, so a heading spread across several columns still sits above them.
Key=

[step]

Say=Very long sheets make long tables; the reader's table commands, such as moving to the first or last row, save a long walk.
Key=

[step]

Say=A deck converted the night before a talk can be studied on a phone, where opening PowerPoint is harder.
Key=

[step]

Say=A presentation's title slide becomes the page's first heading, so the page opens by saying what talk it is.
Key=

[step]

Say=And a workbook's sheets keep their order, so Shift plus H, back by heading, retraces the sheets in the order the author made them.
Key=Shift+H
Hear=Budget, heading level 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Slides by heading, sheets as tables: two kinds of Office file, read without Office open. The next walk converts a whole folder.
Key=
